{{Quote|Those things were floating death traps!|B1 battle droid R0-GR, on STAPs|<ref name="Droidography">''[[Star Wars: Droidography]]''</ref>}}
The '''Single Trooper Aerial Platform''', or simply '''STAP''', and also known as the '''Single Trooper Aerial Transport'''<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2020">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> was a [[repulsorcraft]] used by the [[Trade Federation]] and later the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. It was often [[pilot]]ed by a single [[B1-series battle droid]] as a reconnaissance and patrol vehicle.

==Characteristics==
[[File:STAP-TCW.png|thumb|left|180px|A STAP in the color scheme of the Confederacy of Independent Systems]]
The STAP was a [[Baktoid Armor Workshop]] product designed by [[Trade Federation]] [[engineer]]s, who were inspired by civilian [[airhook]]s. These similar craft were re-engineered for greater performance and reliability, and were purpose-built to be [[pilot]]ed by a [[B1-series battle droid]],<ref name="USW" /> as their [[humanoid]] frames were more suited to control the vehicles.<ref name="SWE STAP">{{SWE|technology|stap|STAP}}</ref> Slim and lightweight, the tiny [[Repulsorcraft|repulsorlift craft]] was fueled by high-voltage [[energy cell]]s, which powered [[drive turbine]]s providing the STAP with impressive speed and maneuverability. The agile vessels were typically bolstered by signals from an orbital [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]], which skillfully guided the STAP's pilots. However, [[battle droid]]s were exposed to enemy fire while riding the fragile craft. The vehicles were armed with a pair of forward-mounted [[blaster cannon]]s.<ref name="USW" />

==Role==
Designed as a reliable reconnaissance and patrol vehicle, the STAP was typically deployed by the [[Trade Federation]] [[Trade Federation Droid Army|Droid Army]] at landing zones where their pilots could survey the area and transmit data back to a [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]].<ref name="USW" /> STAPS were often deployed as support vehicles alongside other, larger craft<ref name="Databank" /> which bore the brunt of combat, and only occasionally forayed into battle in order to harry enemy forces. STAPS were also utilized for "mopping up" missions once a battle was finished.<ref name="USW" />

==History==
===Service in the Invasion of Naboo===
[[File:ST-STAPs.jpg|thumb|right|250px|B1 battle droids riding STAPs over the plains of Naboo]]
The [[Trade Federation]] deployed STAPs alongside its invasion forces during the [[Invasion of Naboo|blockade of]] [[Naboo]]. Numerous STAPs patrolled the swamps surrounding the landing zone, and accompanied [[Multi-Troop Transport]]s into the [[city]] of [[Theed]], where [[Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]] declared victory and occupation. The [[Jedi]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] were harried by STAPs in the swamps, but Jinn destroyed the vehicles by deflecting their pilots' [[blaster]] bolts back into the craft with his [[lightsaber]].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> STAPs surveyed the [[Great Grass Plains]] and transmitted data back to the orbital [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]].<ref name="USW" />

During the [[Battle of Naboo]], B1s on STAPs flew over the Great Grass Plains after the defeat of the [[Gungan Grand Army]]. Shortly afterward, however, the entire droid army was shut down when the [[Force-sensitive]] pilot [[Anakin Skywalker]] destroyed the Droid Control Ship.<ref name="TPM" />

===Service in the Clone Wars===
{{Quote|I'm still convinced more battle droids were destroyed by STAPs than by Jedi during the Clone Wars—and we were the ones flying the darn things.|R0-GR|<ref name="Droidography" />}}
[[File:DroidsSTAPsHissrich-JOTRMaceWindu2.png|thumb|left|330x570px|STAPs served in major battles for the Separatist Alliance.]]
STAPs were later used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Databank" /> a [[The galaxy|galactic]] war between the Confederacy and [[Galactic Republic]]. During the final stages of the [[Battle of Christophsis]], several STAPs patrolled the landing zone of [[General]] [[Whorm Loathsom]]'s<ref name="The Hidden Enemy">{{TCW|The Hidden Enemy}}</ref> newly arrived [[Whorm Loathsom's army|droid army]],<ref name="The Hidden Enemy original guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode016.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: The Hidden Enemy}}</ref> with [[Jedi General]]s Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker stealing two of the vehicles from their B1 pilots to return to the [[Christophsis Republic base|Republic frontline]].<ref name="The Hidden Enemy" />

After the Republic victory on [[Christophsis]], Skywalker and his [[501st Legion]] were rerouted to the [[Wild Space]] world of [[Teth]] to rescue the [[Reproduction|son]] of [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], [[Rotta]]. Seeking to protect their captive, a detachment of the [[Separatist Droid Army]] was stationed on-world, defending the [[B'omarr Order Monastery]] they were using to hold the infant. During the ensuing [[Battle of Teth]], B1s on STAPs made attack runs against the 501st, but Skywalker cut down a number of the B1 pilots before stealing one of the STAPs, using it to reach the top of the mountain.<ref name="The Clone Wars (film)">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref> Additionally, at least one STAP was used by a B1 during the [[Battle of Mimban]], flying against [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex|CT-7567]] "Rex" and [[Junior Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] when they journeyed to take out a [[deflector shield generator]]. Firing one of his [[DC-17 repeater hand blaster|DC-17 hand blasters]] at it, Rex took out the STAP.<ref name="501 Plus One">{{StoryCite|story=501 Plus One|book=Age of Republic Special 1}}</ref>

Later in [[21 BBY]],<ref name="21 BBY Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of "[[Blue Shadow Virus (episode)|Blue Shadow Virus]]" to [[21 BBY]].</ref> while the Separatists worked on a secret effort to recreate the deadly [[Blue Shadow Virus]] on Naboo, a squad of B1-mounted STAPs were led by [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|T-series unit]] [[TR-350]] to contain a small amount of the [[disease]] that had leaked out. However, the squad was attacked by [[Royal Naboo Security Forces]], leading to the capture of TR-350 and a [[Raid on Nuvo Vindi's laboratory|raid on the Separatist laboratory]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus">{{TCW|Blue Shadow Virus (episode)}}</ref> Later, STAPs patrolled the energy bridge into the [[Battle of Ryloth|occupied]] [[capital]] of [[Ryloth]], [[Lessu City|Lessu]], and Jedi [[General]] [[Mace Windu]] jumped off one of the vehicles in order to get over the gap the bridge had covered.<ref name="Liberty on Ryloth">{{TCW|Liberty on Ryloth}}</ref> STAPs also served as patrols at the [[Citadel]] on [[Lola Sayu]], being flown by [[BX-series droid commando]]s and [[Warden]] [[Osi Sobeck]] in a failed attempt to stop a [[Battle of Lola Sayu|Republic infiltration]].<ref name="Citadel Rescue">{{TCW|Citadel Rescue}}</ref>

At one point, an [[Umbaran]] [[officer]] commanded a force of the [[Separatist Droid Army]] that included STAPs.<ref name="Collapse">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> General [[Grievous]], [[Supreme Martial Commander of the Separatist Droid Armies|Supreme Commander of the Droid Army]], utilized a [[combat speeder]] that was bulkier than the standard STAP.<ref name="Grievous' Speeder">{{Databank|general-grievous-speeder|General Grievous' Speeder}}</ref> During the Separatist [[Invasion of Florrum|takeover]] of [[Florrum]], Grievous led a team of STAPs aboard his [[Grievous's Combat speeder|combat speeder]] against a [[WLO-5 speeder tank|WLO-5 battle tank]] used by [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]].<ref name="ANB">{{TCW|A Necessary Bond}}</ref> On [[Utapau]] while trying to [[Mission to Utapau|reclaim]] a massive [[kyber crystal]] from Skywalker and Kenobi, [[IG-100 MagnaGuard]]s rode on STAPs to chase them.<ref name="Crystal Crisis">{{TCW|Crystal Crisis}}</ref> STAPs rode by B1 droids were also part of the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]].<ref name="First Blood 4">[[Kanan 10|''Kanan'' 10]]</ref>

===After the war===
{{Quote|They are antiques, remnants of the Clone War.|Senior Lieutenant Thrawn collected pieces of Clone Wars technology, including half of a STAP|<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref>}}
[[File:ThrawnAndRossi-Thrawn2.png|thumb|right|340x341px|Senior Lieutenant Thrawn and Captain Filia Rossi came to discuss the purpose of the former's collection of Clone Wars technology.]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], half of a STAP was among various pieces of technology leftover from the Clone Wars in a scrap market. When the [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]] ''[[Blood Crow]]'' investigated the market for [[Smuggler|smuggling]] activity, [[Senior Lieutenant]] and [[first weapons officer]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]] "Thrawn" found the antiques and sought to learn more about the technology of the Clone Wars-era by studying and possibly repairing them. Purchasing them with five hundred of his own [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] after [[Captain]] [[Rik Virgilio]] allowed him to, Thrawn stored the STAP and the other pieces of technology in a part of the Gozanti's storage bay he was permitted to when he was not working on them. However, after [[Filia Rossi]] became captain of the ''Blood Crow'', Senior [[Lieutenant]] [[Nels Deyland]] told her of Thrawn's collection, so she confronted the [[Chiss]] officer about the objects.<ref name="Thrawn" />

Looking at the STAP and everything else he had gathered, Virgilio considered the entire assortment to be garbage and ordered Thrawn to get rid of it all before his next watch, furthering telling Deyland to make sure it was done. Even so, Deyland was interested when Thrawn proposed another solution, leading to Rossi allowing him to speak and discuss how the lot had been worth five hundred credits because of the presence of [[Mark One Pistoeka sabotage droid]]s. Learning of the value in such units, she gave Thrawn three [[Standard month|months]] to work on the technology before she took it when they returned to [[Ansion]]. Thrawn's [[aide]], [[Ensign]] [[Eli N. Vanto]], was surpirsed Rossi allowed him to keep the assortment until Thrawn noted she would take it. Ultimately, however, Rossi would suspend Thrawn from duty aboard the ''Blood Crow'' after his [[Dromedar hijacking|mission]] on the ''[[Dromedar]]'', sending Vanto away with him.<ref name="Thrawn" />

==Behind the scenes==
Single Trooper Aerial Platforms first appeared in the [[prequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']],<ref name="TPM" /> which released on [[May 19]], [[1999]].<ref name="YBY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> The vehicle was first identified as "Single Trooper Aerial Platform" in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] by the [[StarWars.com]] now-defunct [[Encyclopedia (StarWars.com)|Encyclopedia]].<ref name="SWE STAP" />

